    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi,<br><br>Is there a plan to describe the latest changes to the mapping algorithm used in version 1.5.0? According to the <a href=\"http://subread.sourceforge.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://subread.sourceforge.net/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3TLAofIGkW8H7PhsqnRPkK\">SourceForge</a> page, there are two main new updates to subread-align:<br><ul><li>New parameter &#39;--type&#39; for sequencing-type-specific mapping optimization.</li><li>Improved detection of multi-mapping reads by considering locations that receive second highest votes.</li></ul>But I couldn&#39;t find anywhere in the <a href=\"http://bioinf.wehi.edu.au/subread-package/SubreadUsersGuide.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://bioinf.wehi.edu.au/subread-package/SubreadUsersGuide.pdf&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw38gUIYzNoeriWsYWadYEOJ\">Users Guide</a> that details the new features and how they will affect mapping results.<br><br>I noticed that there were a decent number of differences in my mapping results obtained from v1.4.4 and v1.5.0. I&#39;ve cherry-picked a few examples from the mapping of the fastq file from my last <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/forum/#!topic/subread/gueV7zD37GY\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/forum/%23!topic/subread/gueV7zD37GY&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571907000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1E-fe9Va1OYrfpvJnjKTV0\">post</a>. Below are links to the bam files.<br><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/1v3ngtnb4ljkkcj/test-pass-v1.4.4.bam?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/1v3ngtnb4ljkkcj/test-pass-v1.4.4.bam?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571908000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1dvqyT2qylcx5vbWnvtm8M\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/1v3ngtnb4ljkkcj/test-pass-v1.4.4.bam?dl=0</a><br><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/fk61awkum3jecf4/test-pass-v1.5.0.bam?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.dropbox.com/s/fk61awkum3jecf4/test-pass-v1.5.0.bam?dl%3D0&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571908000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2RYi96ZXJzsXNpmAC_PPz3\">https://www.dropbox.com/s/fk61awkum3jecf4/test-pass-v1.5.0.bam?dl=0</a><br><br>To find differences, I ran the following:<br><br>diff &lt;(samtools view test-pass-v1.4.4.bam | cut -f1-4) &lt;(samtools view test-pass-v1.5.0.bam | cut -f1-4) &gt; test-pass-diff.txt<br><br>Below are a few different examples. I&#39;d appreciate any insight into how the latest changes result in the different mappings.<br><br># Example 1 - Two different mapping locations<br><br>From the diff file:<br><br>&lt; HWI-700819F:305:C723YACXX:2:2101:19408:54948:UMI_GACGAGGG    16    chr17    44799478<br>---<br>&gt; HWI-700819F:305:C723YACXX:2:2101:19408:54948:UMI_GACGAGGG    0    chr2    3623180<br><br>Obtaining the sequence:<br><br>zcat test-pass.fastq.gz | grep HWI-700819F:305:C723YACXX:2:2101:19408:54948:UMI_GACGAGGG -A 3<br>@HWI-700819F:305:C723YACXX:2:2101:19408:54948:UMI_GACGAGGG 1:N:0:GTCAATCC<br>AAGCCGGCGCTCGGCAAGTTCTCCCAGGAGAAAGCCATGTTCAGTTCGAGCGCCAAGATCGTGAAGCCCAATGGCGAGAAGCCGGACGAGTT<br>+<br>FFFFFFIFIIFIIIIIIIFIIIIIIIIFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFBBFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFBBFFFBBBBBBBBFFFFBBBFFFFFFFFF&lt;B<br><br>When I BLAT this read against hg19 on the UCSC Genome Browser, I found that the new result from 1.5.0 is more accurate (the top hit). The result from v1.4.4 is the third best hit with BLAT.<br><br>\r\n<tt><pre>   ACTIONS      QUERY           SCORE START  END QSIZE IDENTITY CHRO STRAND  START    END      SPAN\r\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n<a href=\"https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position=chr2:3622923-3623255&amp;db=hg19&amp;ss=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx+../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa&amp;hgsid=459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position%3Dchr2:3622923-3623255%26db%3Dhg19%26ss%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx%2B../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa%26hgsid%3D459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571908000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1nrJ3E2P-OpvCNjnJC2CKC\">browser</a> <a href=\"https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o=3622922&amp;g=htcUserAli&amp;i=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx+..%2Ftrash%2FhgSs%2FhgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa+YourSeq&amp;c=chr2&amp;l=3622922&amp;r=3623255&amp;db=hg19&amp;hgsid=459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgc?o%3D3622922%26g%3DhtcUserAli%26i%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx%2B..%252Ftrash%252FhgSs%252FhgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa%2BYourSeq%26c%3Dchr2%26l%3D3622922%26r%3D3623255%26db%3Dhg19%26hgsid%3D459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793234571908000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3oQsgS6uk42UppSI55nZpw\">details</a> YourSeq           91     1    92    92 100.0%     2   +    3622923   3623255    333\r\n<a href=\"https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position=chr17:26794804-26794895&amp;db=hg19&amp;ss=../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx+../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa&amp;hgsid=459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.genome.ucsc.edu/cgi-bin/hgTracks?position%3Dchr17:26794804-26794895%26db%3Dhg19%26ss%3D../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.pslx%2B../trash/hgSs/hgSs_www_db2_88d040.fa%26hgsid%3D459042691_KYaAi2Aus3nZA1YLXEhvkcvRJymO&amp;source=gmai