   "subject": "Re: Differences in mapping algorithm in version 1.5.0",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>We will add more detailed descriptions to the &#39;--type&#39; parameter and also to our recent improvement on mapping multi-mapping reads in the users guide in the next release.<br><br>It has been nearly two years between the releases of versions 1.4.4 and 1.5.0, so there will be some differences between them. It is good to see v1.5.0 gave you better mapping result compared to v1.4.4 in your Example #1.<br><br>For your example #2, although the read was mapped to chr2 by v1.5.0, it was mapped to a location different from that reported by BLAT. You will need to check the CIGAR string reported by 1.5.0 to see how many bases were successfully aligned in the read. I bet it should a lot more than 20.<br><br>For example #3, it is hard to tell what caused the 1 base difference in mapping location without seeing the CIGAR strings. This could be caused by soft-clipping or presence of an indel. Again, it will be helpful if you can show the CIGAR for these mappings.<br><br>Cheers,<br>Wei<br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
